Clickable status blocks. The status text names a block with ^a<name>^ and
ends it with ^a^, codes status2d.diff's parser now skips; dwm notes where
each named block is drawn. A click on one runs its command from
statusactions (config.h) with sh, which gets the block's left and right
edges, the screen's right edge, the bar's bottom and the mouse button as
$1 to $5: enough to open a dropdown under the block, or to act on a
scroll. A click outside any named block does what it did. slstatus/config.h
names the blocks. Applies after launch.diff.

